{
  "info": {
    "name": "Parent Onboarding API Collection",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json",
    "version": "1.0.0",
    "description": "EduPulse auth-service — Parent Onboarding (docs/API_V4.0_PARENT_ONBOARDING.md), Phase 5: parent account activation.\nImplemented so far: Step 1 (invite verify) and Steps 2/3 (OTP send/verify, reused). Steps 4-6 (onboarding-options, profile, set-password) and Phase 6 (login) are not yet built — this collection stops once both OTP channels are verified.\n\nThis collection includes its own 'Prerequisite' folder (teacher login + invite a parent) so it's self-contained — see postman_parent_invite_collection.json for the full teacher-facing invite flow (single/bulk/template) on its own.\n\nBefore running:\n1. {{teacher_email}} / {{teacher_password}} must belong to an already-activated teacher account for {{branch_id}} (see postman_teacher_onboarding_collection.json to create one).\n2. {{class_id}}, {{section_id}}, {{relationship_type_id}} must be filled in manually. Grab sample ids with:\n   SELECT id, name FROM masters.classes;\n   SELECT id, name FROM masters.sections;\n   SELECT id, name FROM masters.relationship_type;\n   against the tenant DB.\n3. The raw parent invite token is never returned by the API — after 'Invite a Parent' below, copy it from the auth-service console log line `[DEV] parent raw invite token: ...` into {{parent_invite_token}}.\n4. OTP codes are never returned by the API either — point OMNICHANNEL_URL at a real service, or run a throwaway local listener on port 8009 that logs the POST body of /api/v1/notify, and read the code from the message text into {{otp}}."
  },
  "variable": [
    { "key": "base_url", "value": "http://localhost:8080" },
    { "key": "chain_id", "value": "bbbbbbbb-0001-4000-8000-000000000001" },
    { "key": "branch_id", "value": "dddddddd-0001-4000-8000-000000000001" },

    { "key": "teacher_email", "value": "" },
    { "key": "teacher_password", "value": "" },
    { "key": "teacher_access_token", "value": "" },

    { "key": "student_name", "value": "Kavin Raj" },
    { "key": "class_id", "value": "" },
    { "key": "section_id", "value": "" },
    { "key": "parent_name", "value": "Suresh Raj" },
    { "key": "parent_email", "value": "suresh.raj@example.com" },
    { "key": "parent_mobile", "value": "+919876500011" },
    { "key": "relationship_type_id", "value": "" },

    { "key": "parent_invite_token", "value": "" },
    { "key": "temp_token", "value": "" },
    { "key": "otp", "value": "" }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "0 — Prerequisite: Invite a Parent (Teacher)",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Teacher Login",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "const res = pm.response.json();",
                  "if (res.success && res.data) {",
                  "    pm.collectionVariables.set('teacher_access_token', res.data.access_token);",
                  "    console.log('teacher token saved');",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"{{teacher_email}}\",\n  \"password\": \"{{teacher_password}}\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/auth/login",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
              "path": ["auth", "login"]
            },
            "description": "Needs an already-activated teacher account for {{branch_id}} (see postman_teacher_onboarding_collection.json)."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Invite a Parent",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "const res = pm.response.json();",
                  "if (res.success && res.data) {",
                  "    console.log('status:', res.data.status, '-', res.data.message);",
                  "    if (res.data.status === 'invited') {",
                  "        console.log('Now copy the raw token from the auth-service console log line: [DEV] parent raw invite token: ... into parent_invite_token');",
                  "    }",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" },
              { "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{teacher_access_token}}" },
              { "key": "chain_id", "value": "{{chain_id}}", "description": "Required — TenantDB middleware uses this to load the correct DB pool." }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"student_name\": \"{{student_name}}\",\n  \"class_id\": \"{{class_id}}\",\n  \"section_id\": \"{{section_id}}\",\n  \"parent_name\": \"{{parent_name}}\",\n  \"parent_email\": \"{{parent_email}}\",\n  \"parent_mobile\": \"{{parent_mobile}}\",\n  \"relationship_type_id\": \"{{relationship_type_id}}\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/teacher/parents/invite",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
              "path": ["teacher", "parents", "invite"]
            },
            "description": "One invite always covers exactly one student. See postman_parent_invite_collection.json for the full invite flow (single/bulk/template) on its own."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Phase 5 — Parent Account Activation",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Step 1 — Invite Verify",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "const res = pm.response.json();",
                  "if (res.success && res.data && res.data.temp_token) {",
                  "    pm.collectionVariables.set('temp_token', res.data.temp_token);",
                  "    console.log('temp_token saved:', res.data.temp_token);",
                  "    console.log('student:', JSON.stringify(res.data.student));",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"token\": \"{{parent_invite_token}}\",\n  \"chain_id\": \"{{chain_id}}\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/parent-auth/invite/verify",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
              "path": ["parent-auth", "invite", "verify"]
            },
            "description": "Validates the magic link — rejects a teacher/tenant_admin/chain_admin token (target_role filter).\nMarks the invite accepted and opens a 20-minute Redis session scoped to the one student this invite covers.\nReturns temp_token + masked parent info + the single linked student (id/name/class/section/relationship)."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Step 2a — OTP Send (SMS)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"temp_token\": \"{{temp_token}}\",\n  \"channel\": \"sms\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/auth/otp/send",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
              "path": ["auth", "otp", "send"]
            },
            "description": "Reused endpoint — identical behavior for every role. No code change was needed for the parent role; it works because Step 1 populates the session's phone/email."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Step 3a — OTP Verify (SMS)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"temp_token\": \"{{temp_token}}\",\n  \"channel\": \"sms\",\n  \"otp\": \"{{otp}}\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/auth/otp/verify",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
              "path": ["auth", "otp", "verify"]
            },
            "description": "Sets sms_verified = true in the Redis session."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Step 2b — OTP Send (Email)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"temp_token\": \"{{temp_token}}\",\n  \"channel\": \"email\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/auth/otp/send",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
              "path": ["auth", "otp", "send"]
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Step 3b — OTP Verify (Email)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"temp_token\": \"{{temp_token}}\",\n  \"channel\": \"email\",\n  \"otp\": \"{{otp}}\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/auth/otp/verify",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
              "path": ["auth", "otp", "verify"]
            },
            "description": "Sets email_verified = true. Phase 5 Steps 4-6 (onboarding-options, profile, set-password) aren't built yet — this is as far as the flow goes for now."
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
